Answers files for the unattended installer.

Each file is plain shell, sourced by kldload-install-target under `set -a`, so
every assignment becomes an environment variable. Anything the guided
installer asks, an answers file can state.

Two ways one reaches a machine:

  USB      ./deploy.sh seed-disk --answers <file> --device /dev/sdX
           writes a 32 MB FAT32 volume labelled KLDLOAD-SEED holding
           answers.env. kldload-autoinstall finds it by label.

  Netboot  serve the file over HTTP and put its URL on the kernel cmdline as
           kldload.seed=http://host/answers/<mac>.env — checked BEFORE the
           seed disk, because a cmdline is per-boot intent and a forgotten
           stick in the front panel is not.

KLDLOAD_DISK may be left empty: the installer picks the first disk that is
neither the live medium nor the seed disk. Set it explicitly on any machine
with more than one candidate.
